‘I’m sorry.’ Hannah breathed deeply, trying to put a halt to the fear that threatened to freeze her ‘I just–’
‘You don’t need to apologise to me.’ Laura husked, pressing a tender kiss to her mouth. ‘Just you and me, remember.’
‘You and me.’ Hannah nodded. Leaning forward to kiss her again.


